+{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"9ce4e24f-6350-465f-bac3-fdae97f6e9f7","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The workspace is set up with package.json, tsconfig.json, eslint config, and vitest config. The src directory is empty except for .gitkeep. I need to install dependencies and build the entire application.\n\nLet me plan the implementation:\n\n1. Install npm dependencies\n2. Create the application structure:\n   - `src/index.ts` or `src/app.ts` - main entry with `createApp()` export\n   - Types/interfaces\n   - In-memory storage\n   - Auth middleware\n   - Routes for users, folders, documents, sharing, activity\n3. Write tests\n4. Verify `npm run build`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`\n\nLet me think about the architecture:\n\n**Data Models:**\n- User: { id, username, password (hashed), createdAt }\n- Folder: { id, name, parentId (optional), ownerId, createdAt, updatedAt }\n- Document: { id, title, content, folderId, ownerId, createdAt, updatedAt }\n- Share: { id, resourceType ('folder'|'document'), resourceId, userId, role ('viewer'|'editor'|'owner'), sharedBy, createdAt }\n- ActivityLog: { id, actionType, userId, targetType, targetId, details, timestamp }\n\n**Auth:**\n- Simple token-based auth: generate a token on login, store token→userId mapping\n- For simplicity, I'll use a random UUID as token\n\n**Permission resolution:**\n- For a document: check direct shares, then check the parent folder's shares (and recursively up)\n- For a folder: check direct shares, then check parent folder's shares (recursively)\n- The creator is always the owner\n\n**API Routes:**\n- POST /api/auth/register - register user\n- POST /api/auth/login - login\n- POST /api/folders - create folder\n- GET /api/folders/:id - get folder\n- PUT /api/folders/:id - update folder\n- DELETE /api/folders/:id - delete folder (recursive)\n- GET /api/folders/:id/children - list children\n- POST /api/documents - create document\n- GET /api/documents/:id - get document\n- PUT /api/documents/:id - update document\n- DELETE /api/documents/:id - delete document\n- POST /api/shares - share a resource\n- GET /api/shares/:resourceType/:resourceId - get shares for a resource\n- DELETE /api/shares/:id - remove a share\n- PUT /api/shares/:id - update a share's role\n- GET /api/activity - get activity log\n\nLet me build this step by step. I'll create the files needed.\n\nFor password hashing, since there's no bcrypt in the dependencies, I'll use a simple hash or even plain text for simplicity in-memory. Actually, let me check if crypto is available (it is in Node.js), so I can use crypto.createHash for a simple SHA256.\n\nLet me structure the code:\n\n```\nsrc/\n  app.ts        - Express app setup, createApp()\n  types.ts      - Type definitions\n  storage.ts    - In-memory storage\n  auth.ts       - Auth middleware\n  routes/\n    auth.ts     - Auth routes\n    folders.ts  - Folder routes\n    documents.ts - Document routes\n    shares.ts   - Sharing routes\n    activity.ts - Activity routes\n```\n\nActually, for simplicity and to keep it manageable, let me put it in fewer files. Let me use:\n\n```\nsrc/\n  types.ts\n  store.ts\n  auth.ts\n  routes.ts\n  app.ts\n```\n\nLet me think about the implementation carefully.\n\nFor the permission model:\n- When creating a folder/document, the creator becomes owner automatically\n- Share a resource with another user with a specific role\n- Effective permission = most permissive role across all paths (direct + inherited)\n- Inheritance: documents inherit from their parent folder chain\n\nFor hierarchical folder access:\n- If user A shares folder X with user B as \"viewer\", B can view folder X and all documents inside X\n- If user A also shares a document inside X with B as \"editor\", B's effective permission on that document is \"editor\" (most permissive)\n- This applies recursively for nested folders\n\nLet me implement the permission resolution:\n\n```\nfunction getEffectivePermission(userId, resourceType, resourceId): role | null\n  - Check direct shares for this resource\n  - If resourceType is 'document', also check parent folder shares recursively\n  - If resourceType is 'folder', also check parent folder shares recursively\n  - If user is the resource owner, return 'owner'\n  - Return the most permissive role found\n```\n\nRole hierarchy: viewer < editor < owner\n\nLet me code this up now. I need to be careful with TypeScript and ESLint rules.\n\nLet me think about passwords. The task says \"Register a new user with username and password\" and \"Login to receive an authentication token.\" Since there's no bcrypt or similar in the deps, I'll use Node.js built-in crypto to hash passwords with SHA256.\n\nActually, let me just store passwords in plaintext for simplicity - this is an in-memory demo. Wait, but I should be somewhat realistic. Let me use crypto.createHash('sha256') which is built into Node.js.\n\nFor tokens, I'll generate random UUIDs using crypto.randomUUID() or Math.random(). crypto.randomUUID() is available in Node.js 19+ but since target is ES2022, let me use it.\n\nLet me write the code now.","signature":"9ce4e24f-6350-465f-bac3-fdae97f6e9f7"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":371,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":20608,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fca386d0-50fe-4c31-bb4e-271c0aa76cf1","uuid":"5caaa033-fc05-4f3e-aa23-68b5db02801d"}
